  <running_head>DE CRVCE</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>cero</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Philo {1} item narrans Iudæos</l>
    <l n="2">Alexandriæ in crucem actos à</l>
    <l n="3">Flacco, hoc addit: <i>μετὰ τὸ αἰκίσασθαι</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>ἐν τῷ θεάτρῳ</i> : <i>postquam flagellati</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>fuissent in theatro.</i> Sollennis ergo</l>
    <l n="6">mos, imò lex: &amp; horrendum</l>
    <l n="7">Carmen diserte canebat {2}:</l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Verbera intra aut extra pomœrium:</i> &amp;</l>
    <l n="9">tum denique succinebat: <i>Arbori</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>infelici suspendito.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="1" caput="3" para="true">CAP. III.</l>
    <l n="12" type="heading" level="2" para="true">
      <i>Flagellorum &amp; Virgarum discri-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>men. Illa magis vilia, &amp; magis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>acerba esse. solere &amp; talis aspe-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="2">
      <i>rari.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Verberati igitur: sed utrùm</l>
    <l n="17">virgis an flagellis? Illas in-</l>
    <l n="18">terdum reperio: sed magis cre-</l>
    <l n="19">brò ista. Discrimen enim esse</l>
    <l n="20">scimus: &amp; quia Virgæ hone-</l>
    <l n="21">stiores, inhonestissimo huic sup-</l>
    <l n="22">plicio adtributa Flagra. Ci-</l>
    <l n="23">cero</l>
    <l n="24" type="foot" para="true">{1} Contra Flaccum.</l>
    <l n="25" type="foot" para="true">{2} Apud Liv. lib. r.</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="left" at="Verberati igitur: sed" line_from="16" line_to="16">Flagra cruciarius propria.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>Left margin note partly damaged; read as "Flagra cruciarius propria." Marginal word-breaks ("crucia-/rius pro-/pria") joined. Greek footnote-line text partly faint; the Greek in the text is uncertain in its final letters. The footnote "lib. r." is doubtful (possibly "lib. I." or "lib. 1.").</notes>
